# TL2: TIMED arm B of the paired ABAB on coding prompts (audits off, the in-trace sampler hang fix kept): A = c2-packed-tp4-best-strace (control), B = c2-packed-tp4-best-lookup; the pair differs in
# QWEN_FAST_LOOKUP_DRAFT alone (test_tp4_lookup_window). Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own all-four reset, same admission order. Runs only if L1 passed (NEEDS in ORDER.txt).
# The tests: warmup and coding (one user), concurrent4_code_equal (four real-code prompts of 4k) and concurrent4_code_32k (four code prompts at 32k, where the user's own context is largest and a
# lookup has the most to copy from).
# READ: tau and the round time TOGETHER, per arm (a user's tok/s = tau x 1000 / round_ms from the SAME arm): the '[PACKED-PHASE]' lines (round time at live=4) and, offline,
#   python scripts/ci/lookup_tau_report.py <A results> <B results>      (tau of each arm from the [PACKED] emitted counts, and the B arm's [LOOKUP-ROUND] lines split by source: how often the lookup was
#   used, and what a lookup round and a DFlash2 round committed)
# Exactness offline: compare the two SMOKE_JSON results test by test and user by user (warmup, coding, concurrent4_code_equal users 0-3, concurrent4_code_32k users 0-3): content_sha256, reasoning_sha256,
# completion_tokens and finish must be identical A against B (the verifier decides every token). (speed_window_compare reads matrix-gate trees, which a smoke job does not write.)
# Judge the pair PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians; check the load average around the run and repeat before believing a small gap. No CI pushes while a timed arm runs (CI shares the host). Duration (estimate): 60 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/lookup four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lookup and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lookup-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/lookup commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lookup-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-lookup
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent4_code_32k
